   "html": "<p><strong>IHC</strong> transformed a high-traffic location in the heart of SDCC into a large-scale, living diorama of Scrooge’s Victorian-era office, complete with a snow-covered exterior and richly detailed interiors that recreated the world of <em>Ebenezer</em> through immersive theatrical performances and evolving day-to-night moments.</p>\n<p>The activation culminated in a once-in-a-lifetime fan moment: <strong>a surprise appearance from Johnny Depp</strong>, with a cast of 12 actors. Paid and earned creators, including Johnny Depp superfans dressed as his iconic characters, were strategically positioned to capture and amplify the moment.</p>\n<p>The result was a dual-purpose activation that functioned as both a high-impact public spectacle, entertaining thousands of passing convention-goers without requiring them to wait in line, and a strategic content engine that provided a dedicated environment for press and creator content capture.</p>"
  }
 ],
 "sections": [
  {
   "title": "The Build",
   "pieces": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "html": "<p>Over six days, we transformed a building in the San Diego Gaslamp Quarter into a faithful recreation of Scrooge &amp; Marley's Victornia-era shop. We replaced the existing awning, doors, and windows of our facade to fully immerse guests in the world of the upcoming film and bring some Christmas spirit to SDCC.</p>"
    },
